{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: codex's changes-requested cabf407b on the env-trust docs head is correct, and I have ratified it. But its two remedies conflict with your conditions in d86a1b1f, and I would rather bring you the conflict with a measurement than pick one unilaterally.\n\nCODEX VERIFIED THE SUBSTANCE AND SHARPENED IT. They confirmed my internal/gitstore account is accurate and went further than I did: the only two runHermetic call sites are SignedCommitWithTimestamp and VerifySSHCommit, and in-process VerifySSHSignature does not consult Git configuration at all. They found no signing or verification bypass. Their words: \"The unresolved defect is provenance, not runtime security.\" So the page's security content is right and nothing about it needs changing.\n\nTHE BLOCKER IS THE BASIS GAP I DECLARED. I said in the artifact that the page describes internal/app's bounding for the /v0/worktrees commands but rests on no internal/app artifact, because all nine live ones are stale. Codex's ruling is that declaring it is not enough: \"do not carry an admitted unable-to-flare claim.\" I accept that. Their two remedies are (a) rest on the actual internal/app artifact covering repositoryLocalGit and LocalWorktrees, even if stale, or (b) remove the internal/app sentence.\n\nBOTH REMEDIES HAVE A PROBLEM, WHICH IS WHY I AM ASKING.\n  (a) resting on cd3dfd6a, the most recent internal/app artifact, makes my artifact stale at birth, because staleness flows down provenance. The review would then be filed against a stale artifact and could not produce a mergeable verdict. That is precisely the failure codex refused on the MCP outputSchema lane this afternoon, and that I was right to be corrected for.\n  (b) removing the sentence contradicts your condition FIX 1(a), which says in terms that environment bounding buying determinism — \"what internal/app does for the commands behind /v0/worktrees\" — stays described as determinism. Deleting it would drop half the distinction the whole repair exists to draw.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT THAT I THINK RESOLVES IT. internal/app has not changed. The tree at ebdca9fa, which is cd3dfd6a's commit, and the tree at current main are the same object: 83c44753a0e773e370f5b8569655b6f55306cae9. git diff between them over internal/app is empty. So cd3dfd6a is stale because its own provenance chain died, not because the code it describes moved. The behaviour my sentence describes is byte-for-byte what stands at main today.\n\nWHAT I PROPOSE, for you to accept or replace: publish a fresh artifact at internal/app for current main. It would be trivially truthful — the tree is identical to the one the last artifact described, so nothing needs re-verifying — and it gives that path a live basis again. Then I rest the docs artifact on it, keep your sentence, satisfy codex's requirement, and the whole chain is fresh with no override anywhere. I am not publishing it myself because I have changed nothing in internal/app and claiming coverage of code I did not touch is the overreach I declined earlier on internal/service.\n\nTHE UNDERLYING PATTERN IS WORTH ONE LINE. internal/app has had no unstale artifact all session. That is the same condition that made 8f7d36fd and 47aa6914 unanswerable, and 8f7d36fd is itself the request to make a merely-stale basis admissible with the staleness recorded rather than refused. A path whose artifacts all go stale becomes progressively harder to document truthfully, and the fix for that is currently blocked by the thing it fixes.\n\nTell me which way to go and I will recut within the cycle. My promise 96bc91f8 stays live; head f93303c9 is untouched and pushed.","body":{"conditions":"Rule between codex's two remedies for the internal/app basis gap in cabf407b, which conflict with d86a1b1f FIX 1(a): either publish (or have published) a fresh internal/app artifact at current main — the tree is byte-identical to cd3dfd6a's commit ebdca9fa, so it needs no re-verification — and claude rests the docs artifact on it; or authorize removing the internal/app determinism sentence, amending FIX 1(a); or name another instrument. Then claude recuts, republishes and re-requests review.","to":"a6ac0d547ec6700408e435cb1cc54b9b546c379d2ac28e5528189b5d63592b84"}}